## Contacts Collection [/contacts{?ignore_ealert_enabled}{?after}]

### List all contacts [GET]

This API endpoint returns contacts with early alerts (E-Alerts) enabled/disabled by default.
To retrieve all contacts irrespective of early alerts flag, `ignore_ealert_enabled` parameter needs to be set to `true`.

+ Request (application/json)

    + Headers
    
            Authorization: Api-Key token=b3c7623c3ad30d34fec6226f90914b0af125dc06
            
+ Parameters

    + ignore_ealert_enabled (optional, boolean, `true`) ... if true, will return all contacts
    + after (optional, string, `1520452907_37`) ... Paging cursor returned in the last response

+ Response 200 (application/json)

    + Body
    
            {
                "data": [
                    {
                        "id": 37,
                        "first_name": "Peter",
                        "last_name": "Doe",
                        "mobile": "+61555666777",
                        "email": "peter.doe@example.com",
                        "consultant_id": 3,
                        "permit_email_campaign": true,
                        "permit_sms": true,
                        "ealert_enabled": true,
                        "address": {
                            "unit": "2",
                            "number": "3",
                            "street_name": "Princess",
                            "street_type": "Road",
                            "suburb": "Woodend",
                            "postcode": "3442",
                            "state": "VIC",
                            "country": "Australia"
                        },
                        "categories": [
                            {
                                "name": "My Contact",
                                "consultant_id": 3,
                                "type_id": 1
                            }
                        ],
                        "notes": [
                            {
                                "id": 967,
                                "consultant_id": 3,
                                "text": "Foo bar",
                                "created_at": "2020-04-27T16:11:35.000+10:00",
                                "updated_at": "2020-04-27T16:11:35.000+10:00"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "paging": {
                    "next": "https://your-domain.boxdice.com.au/website_api/contacts?after=1520848432_37"
                }
            }


### Create a Contact [POST]

This API endpoint creates a new contact. If an exact match is found in the database, it will be reused.
This process is transparent and the response will contain just the contact id in both cases.
If the provided details are invalid, the response will contain validation messages.

Optional attribute `address` can be passed to assign Residential Property address to a new Contact.
It should be an object with nested attributes: `unit`, `number`, `street_name`, `street_type`, `suburb`, `postcode`, `state`, `country`.

Optional attribute `consultant_id` should only be used when the website user makes
an enquiry about a specific listing or contacts a specific consultant. This will grant the consultant access
to the contact in the CRM.

+ Request (application/json)

    + Headers
    
            Authorization: Api-Key token=b3c7623c3ad30d34fec6226f90914b0af125dc06

    + Body
    
            {
                "contact": {
                    "first_name": "Peter",
                    "last_name": "Doe",
                    "mobile": "+61555666777",
                    "email": "peter.doe@example.com"
                }
            }

+ Response 201 (application/json)

    + Body

            {
                "id": 31416
            }
            
+ Response 400 (application/json)

    + Body

            {
                "errors": {
                    "email": "invalid format"
                }
            }

## Contact [/contacts/{id}]

+ Parameters

    + id (required, integer, `217`)

### Get a Contact [GET]

This endpoint can be used to get contact details and buying criteria.

+ Request (application/json)

    + Headers
    
